re is subjected to 200 atmosphere and then passed over heated catalyst mixture of ZnO and $\\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3$ kept at $573-673 \\mathrm{~K}$. This reaction results the formation of methanol vopours which are then condensed to liquid state.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 2)","_marksId":"67726d09c49e8ef28ee2b3c2"},{"id":17250,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Alcohols Phenols and Ethers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"An unknown alcohol is treated with the \"Lucas reagent\" to determine whether the alcohol is primary, secondary or tertiary. Which alcohol reacts fastest and by what mechanism :","options":["secondary alcohol by $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1$","tertiary alcohol by $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1$","secondary alcohol by $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2$","tertiary alcohol by $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2$"],"answer":1,"solution":"The reaction of alcohol with Lucas reagent is mostly an $\\mathrm{S}_{N}1$ mechanism reaction and the rate of reaction is directly proportional to the carbocation stability formed in the reaction, hence tertiary alcohol will react fastest.","difficulty":"Hard","source":"BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 1)","_marksId":"67726cfcc49e8ef28ee2b35b"},{"id":17251,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Alcohols Phenols and Ethers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"Which will not result in the formation of anisole?","options":["$\\mathrm{PhOH}+\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{Cl} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}{\\longrightarrow}$","$\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{ONa} \\frac{623 \\mathrm{~K}}{300 \\mathrm{~atm}}$","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252Fy-jyFVBV_1rofVOlbFMtU1rzYbtbhxMTIsJ44LMYkLg.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.